Fixes #52266
Closes #59598

- **Attach a windowless console to `serve --service` on Windows 11 24H2+ (`packages/cli/src/services/hidden-console.bun.ts`, `packages/cli/src/server-process.ts`):** `spawnServiceContender` launches `opencode serve --service` with `detached: true` (`DETACHED_PROCESS`), leaving the service with no attached console (`AttachConsole` fails with `ERROR_INVALID_HANDLE`). While Core's `CrossSpawnSpawner` sets `windowsHide: true` (`CREATE_NO_WINDOW`), in-process server plugins and package helpers calling `child_process.execSync`, `Bun.spawn`, or `Bun.$` (which exposes no `windowsHide` option) trigger a visible `CASCADIA_HOSTING_WINDOW_CLASS` / `ConsoleWindowClass` window and `EVENT_SYSTEM_FOREGROUND` focus steal per spawn under `opencode-cli.exe`'s PID. Calling `AllocConsoleWithOptions(ALLOC_CONSOLE_MODE_NO_WINDOW)` after incumbent discovery gives the service a windowless console (`GetConsoleWindow() === 0`) that unhidden children inherit silently.
- **Preserve attached terminals and standard handles (`packages/cli/src/services/hidden-console.bun.ts`, `packages/cli/src/services/hidden-console.node.ts`):** Skip allocation when `GetConsoleProcessList` reports an already-attached console (such as interactive `opencode serve --service` in a terminal), save and restore `STD_INPUT_HANDLE` / `STD_OUTPUT_HANDLE` / `STD_ERROR_HANDLE` around allocation so `Service.ensure`'s startup error pipe remains intact, and keep `#hidden-console` a no-op in the Node SEA build.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  Ensure["Service.ensure<br/>DETACHED_PROCESS (no console)"] --> Incumbent{"Incumbent<br/>running?"}
  Incumbent -- "yes" --> Exit["Exit contender"]
  Incumbent -- "no (Win11 26100+)" --> Alloc["AllocConsoleWithOptions<br/>ALLOC_CONSOLE_MODE_NO_WINDOW<br/>+ restore STD_*_HANDLE"]
  Alloc --> Core["CrossSpawnSpawner<br/>CREATE_NO_WINDOW → HWND 0x0"]
  Alloc --> Plugin["In-process Plugin / Bun.$ / execSync<br/>Inherits service console → HWND 0x0"]
```

```ts
const attached = new Uint32Array(1)
if (kernel32.symbols.GetConsoleProcessList(ptr(attached), 1) > 0) return undefined
const handles = standardHandles.map((id) => [id, kernel32.symbols.GetStdHandle(id)] as const)
const status = kernel32.symbols.AllocConsoleWithOptions(ptr(new Int32Array([2, 0, 0])), null)
handles.forEach(([id, handle]) => {
  if (handle !== invalidHandle) kernel32.symbols.SetStdHandle(id, handle)
})
```

| Caller inside `opencode serve --service` (Win11 `10.0.26300`) | `dev` (`SetWinEventHook` events) | PR (`+ HiddenConsole`) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Core `CrossSpawnSpawner` (`git`, `rg`, `powershell`, `.cmd` shims) | `0` (`HWND 0x0`) | `0` (`HWND 0x0`) |
| Local stdio MCP (`.cmd` / `.exe`, plus child `execSync("git")`) | `0` (`HWND 0x0`) | `0` (`HWND 0x0`) |
| Server plugin `child_process.execSync("git ...")` | `SHOW` + `FOREGROUND` (`CASCADIA_HOSTING_WINDOW_CLASS`) | `0` (`HWND 0x0` inherited) |
| Server plugin `Bun.spawn(["git", ...])` (default) | `SHOW` (`visible = 1`) | `0` (`HWND 0x0` inherited) |
| Server plugin `` Bun.$`git ...` `` (no `windowsHide` API) | `CREATE` (`ConsoleWindowClass`) | `0` (`HWND 0x0` inherited) |

