Closes #55216

- **Scope omitted-range `@` lookup to the active text part (`packages/app/src/composer/editor/actions.ts`):** When `range` is omitted (such as file-tree drops via `addPart` → `draft.addMention(part)` or `@` completions), scan `lastIndexOf("@")` only within the `text` part containing `end` rather than across joined `part.content` strings that include earlier `@mention` tokens.
- **Unify point and boundary mention insertion (`insertMention`):** Track `inserted` like `insertText` so zero-width insertions neither duplicate across adjacent text parts nor no-op when the cursor sits directly before or after a structured mention part.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  A["File drop / @ select<br/>addMention(part)"] --> B["withOffsets(prompt)<br/>find text part at cursor"]
  B -->|"@ found in text part"| C["Replace [part.start + idx .. end]"]
  B -->|"No @ in text part"| D["Insert at [end .. end]"]
  C --> E["insertMention (inserted = true)<br/>single rewrite + withOffsets"]
  D --> E
```

```ts
const prompt = withOffsets(store().prompt)
const length = promptLength(prompt)
const end = range?.end ?? Math.min(store().cursor ?? length, length)

const part = prompt.find(
  (item): item is Extract<ComposerPrompt[number], { type: "text" }> =>
    item.type === "text" && end >= item.start && end <= item.end,
)

const index = part ? part.content.slice(0, end - part.start).lastIndexOf("@") : -1
const start = range?.start ?? (part && index >= 0 ? part.start + index : end)
```

