Fixes #52205

- **Match the app's own loopback port before treating HTTP servers as local (`packages/app/src/runtime/server/registry.tsx`, `runtime.tsx`, `current.tsx`):** `isLocalHost` stripped ports (`split(":")[0]`) and marked every `localhost` / `127.0.0.1` HTTP server as sharing the client's filesystem. With Windows's managed service on port `28894` (`0x70de`) and WSL servers on `49374` (`0xc0de`) or `4096` (`opencode serve`), `ServerConnection.local(conn, ownUrl)` now returns `true` only for the built-in desktop sidecar or a loopback HTTP connection matching the normalized loopback protocol and port of `ownUrl` (`sidecar.http.url ?? canonicalLocalServer`), removing the duplicate `isLocalHost` copy in `runtime.tsx`.
- **Thread `servers.local` / `servers.ownUrl` through workspace selection, reveal, settings, and GUI plugin host refs (`packages/app/src/workspaces/selection/policy.ts`, `picker.tsx`, `dialog.tsx`, `home/projects/reveal.ts`, `settings/surface.tsx`, `runtime/plugin/host-apis.tsx`, `packages/plugin/src/gui/host-apis.ts`):** WSL servers added at `http://localhost:4096` or `http://localhost:49374` open the in-app Linux `DirectoryPickerDialog` (emitting `/home/...` instead of `\\wsl.localhost\...` UNC paths), upload dropped composer files instead of passing raw Windows paths, and hide local Explorer reveal actions while preserving local behavior for the Windows sidecar and the web app's own loopback server.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  A["ServerConnection<br/>sidecar | plugin | http"] --> B{"builtin(conn)?"}
  B -- "yes (:28894 sidecar)" --> E["local = true<br/>Native OS Picker"]
  B -- "no" --> C{"conn.type === 'http'<br/>&& loopbackOrigin(url) === loopbackOrigin(ownUrl)?"}
  C -- "yes (localhost:28894 / web :3000)" --> E
  C -- "no (WSL :4096 / :49374 / plugin / remote)" --> F["local = false<br/>In-App Server Picker (/home/...)"]
```

```ts
function loopbackOrigin(url: string) {
  if (!URL.canParse(url)) return
  const parsed = new URL(url)

  if (parsed.hostname !== "localhost" && parsed.hostname !== "127.0.0.1" && parsed.hostname !== "[::1]") return

  return `${parsed.protocol}//127.0.0.1:${parsed.port || (parsed.protocol === "https:" ? "443" : "80")}`
}

export const local = (conn?: Any, ownUrl?: string) => {
  if (!conn) return false

  if (builtin(conn)) return true

  if (conn.type !== "http" || !ownUrl) return false
  const origin = loopbackOrigin(conn.http.url)

  return !!origin && origin === loopbackOrigin(ownUrl)
}
```

