Fixes #54828
Supersedes #54877

- **Sign bit-3 zip data descriptors (`packages/desktop/src/main/native/logging.ts`):** Pass `{ dataDescriptorSignature: true }` to `@zip.js/zip.js`'s `ZipWriter` so every entry prepends the 4-byte `PK\x07\x08` (`0x08074b50`) signature before `[crc32, compressedSize, uncompressedSize]`.
- **Unblock macOS Finder / `Archive Utility` / `ditto`:** `@zip.js/zip.js` defaults to `dataDescriptor: true` and `dataDescriptorSignature: false`. Central-directory readers (`unzip`, `bsdtar`, Windows Explorer) read sizes from EOF and ignore descriptors, whereas Apple's streaming `BOM.framework` parses sequentially from byte `0` and aborts on the first unsigned descriptor (`Couldn't read pkzip signature`).

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  LH["PK 03 04<br/>Local Header (bit 3 = 1)"] --> DEF["Deflate Payload<br/>manifest.json"]
  DEF --> SIG["50 4B 07 08<br/>PK\x07\x08 (+4 B)"]
  SIG --> DD["CRC-32 + Sizes<br/>(12 B)"]
  DD --> BOM["macOS BOM / Finder / ditto<br/>Streams all entries (exit 0)"]
  EOCD["PK 05 06 + Central Dir"] --> CD["unzip / bsdtar / Explorer<br/>Reads sizes from EOF"]
```

```ts
// Before: 12-byte unsigned descriptor -> ditto: Couldn't read pkzip signature (exit 1)
const writer = new ZipWriter(new BlobWriter("application/zip"))

// After: 16-byte signed descriptor (50 4b 07 08 + crc32 + sizes) -> Finder & ditto extract all files
const writer = new ZipWriter(new BlobWriter("application/zip"), { dataDescriptorSignature: true })
```

