### Test gap and repair constraints

The [core status tests](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/ebdc7d54c0842d96c4bb2fb2bb4be4758f07f255/src/plugin-sdk/command-status.runtime.test.ts#L6-L42) mock both the loader and `createModelSelectionState`; Discord's direct-status tests mock the core helper. They do not exercise the contradictory real loader/selection contracts demonstrated here.

Suggested repair boundary: make the status path consume coherent **read-only** selection facts. Keep real stale-selection and live-authority guards intact for execution paths.

Simply making the references identical is a causal control, not a reviewed production patch. The reused selection routine can also persist model resets and [clear auth overrides](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/ebdc7d54c0842d96c4bb2fb2bb4be4758f07f255/src/auto-reply/reply/model-selection.ts#L533-L556). Any fix should prove that direct status succeeds for valid and unavailable saved profiles without silently modifying durable selections. Clearing the user's profile or globally removing the guard would not address that requirement.

### Impact and severity

Native Discord `/status` is unusable in the affected existing session. The operator reports reliable reproduction; four recent log occurrences were verified. The isolated defect is deterministic with a saved profile and requires no race.

No data loss or credential corruption was observed. This report does not claim that every channel, ordinary text-command route, or status tool uses the same failing composition.

### Related reports and duplicate check

I searched open and closed issues/PRs by the exact error, exception class, core helper/loader names, and recent status/Discord titles, then inspected the closest candidates. I found no matching report of this cloned-entry identity rejection.

- #166985 introduced the relevant guard for preserving temporarily unavailable explicit accounts; its goal and genuine-change protections should be preserved.
- #149343 addresses stale automatic auth **labels**, not rejection before rendering.
- #149892 addresses model thinking defaults in status, not the saved-auth clone guard.
- #135154 addresses genuinely stale dispatch ownership after reset/rotation, not an unchanged cloned snapshot.
- #165950 addresses control-plane request scheduling delays, not this immediate local exception.
- #169181 is a separate Discord **final-delivery actor-hydration** failure, not the native command issue reported here.

No production repair, session reset, credential change, or Gateway restart was performed during this investigation.

