## What Problem This Solves

Closes #182414

When reviewing an image in chat, users can open/copy/download it but cannot compare its browser-rendered pixels against a local reference in place. A model response is not a deterministic pixel check.

## User Impact

Add **Compare images** to existing chat image actions and the image viewer, including narrow screens. Pick one same-size local reference; inspect the changed-pixel count and magenta difference mask, then download the difference PNG. The reference is never attached or sent.

## Why This Change Was Made

Both surfaces share one lazy dialog and capture the existing authorized original-blob reader. Comparison stays in the browser and adds no decoder, backend or plugin API. External image-diff tools solve offline/automated comparison but do not provide this action on the currently authorized chat image. The UI explicitly defines browser color/transparency normalization: this compares Canvas samples, not original file bytes or hidden RGB fidelity.

The lightbox content owner also delegates its existing zoom-control markup to the shared lightbox view so the feature fits the unchanged file-size limit. Product placement is proposed for Control UI owner acceptance.

## Evidence

### Current maintenance — October 29, 2026

**Current-head hosted CI:** all checks completed without failures, including [the required CI gate](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/40812464529/job/123248611795) and Control UI performance. This result is for `164058003149c5668c16f12ff9687e0cf0dc59ef`.

Current head: `164058003149c5668c16f12ff9687e0cf0dc59ef`; integrated upstream main: `a4e20a8b24440efd9b8a1792ce400be85a697080`. An ordinary merge resolves the confirmed catalog conflict while retaining main's composer-menu/permission composition. The zoom-control presentation extraction preserves action order, callbacks, focus registration and live disabled/scale values; no budgets or assertions changed.

- **Real browser acceptance:** clean current head passes Chromium 152.0.7977.64 and Linux WebKit 27.2. Both open the actual authorized chat image, select a local reference, download the difference PNG, and decode the downloaded bytes independently. The mask is 320×180 with exactly 200 changed pixels, opaque magenta inside and transparent outside. Gateway recorder contains zero `chat.send` calls.
- **Controls:** different valid PNG bytes with identical rendered pixels yield zero; wrong dimensions remove the previous download; invalid input recovers; hidden/low-alpha RGB normalization and visible alpha controls pass; Close restores viewer focus; the 390×844 footer stays reachable. WebKit retains the existing `interactive-widget` viewport-parser warnings; no unknown page errors occurred. Theme-attribute checks are surface spot checks, not a theme-persistence claim.
- **Before/after:** the same user flow on clean current main has no Compare images action. The screenshots below were inspected and contain synthetic content only.
- **Focused checks:** current candidate tree passes UI types (supported `tsgo`), focused oxlint/format, native controller ratchets, English catalog verification and whitespace checks. After the zoom extraction, 27 focused image/gallery tests pass in **26.17 s wall**. The earlier 81-test run (image/gallery, catalog and accepted warm-selection regression) passed in **44.03 s wall** at `7942232343b1d89b862842afedfb71cd92556cc2`; the unchanged catalog/session test results retain that SHA. The longer run includes the owning catalog and asynchronous session reconciliation controls.
- **Native build/performance:** Node 26.12.1 with independent frozen pnpm 12.15.0 installs. Candidate and pinned-main builds use the repository's fixed comparison environment; build, precompressed-assets guard and unchanged native performance check pass. Chat boot −202 B gzip, New Session −376 B, startup −4 B and CSS 0 B relative to current main. The final build/check inputs match the committed source tree.
- **Independent review:** complete 11-file range at `7942232` and the final two-file zoom extraction were reviewed independently by another session: no actionable P0–P3 findings. Isolated Codex autoreview was attempted, but HTTP 401 produced `reviewer_unavailable` and no report; this is not a clean CLI review. Hosted review will be requested after current-head CI is available.
- **Not tested:** production Gateway, model, external channel, Mac device or installed-release upgrade; these checks use source UI with synthetic local Gateway/media transport. Built-in UI versus a reusable plugin image-action contract remains a Control UI owner decision. Passing proof/CI does not establish product acceptance.

