## What Problem This Solves

Closes #182409

A screenshot may contain a private detail that the user wants to cover before it becomes a chat attachment. The composer currently offers preview/removal but no way to edit those pixels locally.

## User Impact

Add **Redact image** to ready PNG/JPEG/WebP draft thumbnails. Drag opaque black rectangles, undo, then apply a flattened PNG copy. The draft replaces only that image; siblings remain. The source file stays unchanged. Users must review coverage themselves before sending.

## Why This Change Was Made

Put local raster preparation at the existing draft/payload boundary. The replacement is a new admitted payload identity; cancellation/rejected admission preserves the original, and an accepted replacement releases its old payload. Existing upload policy, pending-byte accounting and draft lifetime remain the owners. External editors can redact files but require leaving this draft; the related text-PII/media-blocking proposal does not edit selected image pixels.

8 files; production +348/−6; tests +110/−0 lines. Product placement is proposed for Control UI owner acceptance.

## Evidence

Current product head: `ded83813ba3b10a2de3365b4d4d6efb49a3060c7` (2026-10-29). Resolved the real conflict with current main `a4e20a8b24440efd9b8a1792ce400be85a697080` using an ordinary merge. The canonical catalog retains main's composer/menu/permissions composition and adds the redaction registrar; the feature remains 8 files, production +348/−6, tests +110/−0. No budget, assertion, translation memory, or baseline allowance was loosened.

**Fresh real UI proof:** Chromium 152 and Linux Playwright WebKit 27.2 both pass on this clean head. Upload the synthetic PNG → open the native modal → drag opaque rectangles → Undo/Cancel/Escape and focus-return controls → Apply → explicit Send → inspect the ordinary `chat.send` recorder payload and independently decode its actual PNG. It contains one new `-redacted.png`, selected sample [0,0,0,255], outside sample [255,255,255,255], 320×180. Cancel preserves the source preview and sends nothing; Undo disables Apply. Light/dark surfaces are checked. Reference files and unrelated external messages are not used.

