**Checks:** frozen-lockfile dependencies; focused formatting/lint, full UI types with the supported tsgo runner, controller shrink-only guard, canonical i18n baseline, native Vite build, and all 2,454 finalized precompression sidecars pass. Native performance comparison against the independently built pinned main above passes unchanged: Chat gzip −275 B (20 requests unchanged); New Session −222 B; startup −4 B; total CSS raw/gzip +0 B. No performance exception was introduced.

**Tests and retained failure:** the 7 redaction admission cases, existing attachment cases, and existing Vite/catalog suite total 76 passing assertions in the frozen-head run (38.19 s wall time), but the combined Node job exits 1 on an unhandled Node/Undici `abortFetch` TypeError (reading `error`) attributed to `chat-attachments.test.tsx`. It is not described as green. The same stack reproduces on independently installed clean pinned main; that base run also has one existing image admission-order timeout. Earlier Node24/26 attempts and their failures remain retained. This PR does not change those fixtures or suppress the failure. The redaction tests cover replacement order/identity, retained sibling bytes, rejected publication cleanup, and disabled/aborted/removed/parked drafts.

**Current-head online CI (2026-10-29):** 112 applicable check runs completed successfully or skipped/neutral; 2 earlier cancelled dispatch/context runs have newer successful replacements. `openclaw/ci-gate`, dependency-review, and security-sensitive-review are successful. The temporary security status has resolved to “No sensitive product changes.” The branch is mergeable without conflicts. Both current-head inline PNG attachments were independently fetched anonymously with HTTP 200, image/png, and byte-identical SHA-256 to the inspected local captures. This does not replace the remaining Control UI product-placement decision.

