## What Problem This Solves

Closes #182410

Creating a quick diagram or spatial instruction currently requires a separate drawing app, an export, and an attachment import. The composer has no blank-canvas input.

## User Impact

Add **Draw a sketch** to the existing attachment menu. Draw, undo or clear, then attach a plain 800×450 PNG. It remains a draft until the user sends it. Blank/Clear disables Attach; Cancel and Escape leave the message unchanged.

## Why This Change Was Made

Reuse the existing annotation painter, native promise-modal lifecycle, and ordinary attachment admission/payload owners. A sketch is an ordinary image without browser screenshot context. The current plugin composer contract cannot stage a file into the built-in composer.

The current main menu split is preserved, including native mobile file selection and media inputs. Its attachment rows and selection handling now share one focused module; this keeps the main menu body below its existing 700-line limit. Sketch code loads only on invocation. No backend, settings, protocol or persisted format changes.

10 files; production +405/−95 and tests +83/−1 lines. **Product placement still needs a Control UI owner decision:** this PR proposes a built-in composer attachment action; it does not claim that design has been accepted.

## Evidence

Current head: `2589adb482b570a3b39114003acbd115ed5fde16`. Integrated main: `a4e20a8b24440efd9b8a1792ce400be85a697080`, using an ordinary merge to resolve actual conflicts and retaining the original history.

**Before:** On the clean current-main composer, Camera/Media/File options are present and there is no Draw a sketch action. The same browser collector's acceptance-red records this capability gap on `a4e20a8b24440efd9b8a1792ce400be85a697080`.

![Before: current main attachment menu without a sketch action](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/42293156-d8d8-42a4-a76c-7915a2a49978)

**After:** Fresh Chromium and Linux Playwright WebKit runs at the clean current head draw two strokes, undo the second, attach, and explicitly send. The actual captured chat.send contains one sketch.png; independent PNG decode reads 800×450, retained pixel [224,68,45,255], and undone/background pixels [255,255,255,255].

![After: current-head sketch with one retained stroke](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c9cc7f7d-b546-4bb4-b0a6-d3274c6ac4a9)

**Controls:** Blank and Clear disable Attach. Cancel/Escape leave 0 attachments and 0 sends and restore native focus. Attaching alone leaves 0 sends; the positive explicit-send control records 1 send with 1 image. Theme-attribute spot checks are recorded; they do not establish dark-mode correctness or theme-preference persistence.

